---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/content/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';

const path = '/privacy/';
---
<BaseLayout
  title={`Privacy Policy for ${siteConfig.siteName} Users`}
  description={`Privacy policy for ${siteConfig.siteName}: client-side generators, optional analytics cookies, Google AdSense and Analytics disclosures, and data you control.`}
  path={path}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy', path }]} />
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="content-meta">Last updated: 2026-11-13</p>
  <p>
    {siteConfig.siteName} (“we”) operates {siteConfig.siteUrl}. This policy explains what we collect when you use our website and tools,
    what we do not collect, and how to contact us about privacy requests.
  </p>

  <h2>Document generators (no server storage)</h2>
  <p>
    Form data you enter in our generators is processed in your browser to render previews and exports. We do not transmit your document
    contents to our servers for storage or review. If you click “Save locally,” data is stored in your browser’s localStorage only and
    never leaves your device unless you export or copy it yourself.
  </p>
  <p>
    Because we do not host user-generated contracts or filled forms, a typical privacy request will not involve deleting document text
    from our systems—we usually have none. You can clear local drafts by using each tool’s clear-draft control or by clearing site data
    in your browser.
  </p>

  <h2>Log data</h2>
  <p>
    Our hosting provider (Cloudflare) may log IP addresses, user agents, requested URLs, and similar technical data for security,
    reliability, and abuse prevention. We use these logs for operations—not for building marketing profiles of individuals.
  </p>

  <h2>Google Analytics (optional)</h2>
  <p>
    If enabled, we use Google Analytics 4 to understand aggregate traffic (for example, which tools are opened). Consent Mode v2 keeps
    analytics and ad-related storage denied by default. In the EEA, UK, and Switzerland those defaults are region-scoped and stay denied
    until Google’s certified CMP updates consent. Elsewhere, storage stays denied until you Accept the site cookie bar. The GA script is
    deferred until after page load / idle so it is not render-blocking. You can opt out via browser settings or Google’s tools. Measurement
    ID is configured in site settings. We may record events such as opening a tool editor, exporting PDF/DOCX, copying an embed snippet,
    and clicking outbound reference links.
  </p>

  <h2>Google AdSense and advertising cookies</h2>
  <p>
    If we display Google AdSense ads, Google and its partners may use cookies (or similar technologies) to serve ads based on your prior
    visits to this or other websites. Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads. You can opt out of personalized
    advertising by visiting
    <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a> and
    <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info/" rel="noopener noreferrer">aboutads.info</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    For visitors in the EEA, UK, and Switzerland, personalized ads use Google’s certified AdSense GDPR consent message (Privacy &amp;
    messaging / Funding Choices, IAB Transparency and Consent Framework v2.2), loaded with the AdSense script. That message is the consent
    UI for those regions; the site’s own cookie bar is not shown there. See <a href="/cookies/">our cookie notice</a> for which tool
    applies where.
  </p>
  <p>
    AdSense is controlled by site configuration (<code>PUBLIC_ADS_ENABLED</code> and a publisher ID). When ads are off, we do not load the
    AdSense script (and therefore do not show Google’s CMP message).
  </p>

  <h2>Contact form</h2>
  <p>
    If the contact form is enabled, messages you send are delivered through our email provider (EmailJS on the free plan uses their
    servers to route mail). Do not include confidential client contracts or sensitive personal data you would not put in an ordinary email.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>This site is intended for business users and is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy when our tools, hosting, or advertising setup changes. The “Last updated” date at the top reflects the latest
    revision. Continued use of the site after changes means you have read the updated policy.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Privacy questions:
    <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a>
    or use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> with “Privacy” in the subject line.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
